-- title:
--   Sdd Op Rel Swap Questions
-- statement:
--   **Uniform slice-pair operator relations survive swapping the two question coordinates.**
--
--   Let `A` and `B` be indexed operator families on slice-pair questions. If they satisfy `SDDOpRel` with error `delta` under the uniform slice-pair distribution, then the families reindexed by `q -> (q.2,q.1)` satisfy the same relation under the same distribution:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}(\psi,\mathcal D,A,B,\delta)
--   \Longrightarrow
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}(\psi,\mathcal D,\operatorname{swap}A,\operatorname{swap}B,\delta).
--   $$
--
--   The proof is a finite reindexing by `Prod.swap`; uniformity makes the distribution invariant. This utility supplies the orientation change needed by the complete-part commuting-with-G construction.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.sddOpRel_swap_questions`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
